Package: quicopt
Title: Client for the 'Quicopt' Optimization Service
Version: 0.4.0
Authors@R: person("Tim", "Bode", email = "t.bode@fz-juelich.de",
                  role = c("aut", "cre", "cph"))
Description: Write an optimization model in R and solve it with the
    'Quicopt' service <https://quicopt.com>: state the decisions, the
    objective and the constraints, and the service finds the best decision.
    The model is sent to the service, so no solver needs to be installed.
    Uncertain data, such as demand or prices, is described by probability
    distributions or taken from the rows of a data frame, and the model can
    then minimize an expected cost, guard against bad outcomes, or require a
    condition to hold with a given probability. Decisions that are an order
    or an assignment, such as a delivery route, can be stated directly.
License: Apache License (== 2.0)
Encoding: UTF-8
Imports: curl, jsonlite, utils
Suggests: knitr, rmarkdown
VignetteBuilder: knitr
Depends: R (>= 4.1)
